text:
Point S has coordinates (5, −3).

Point S is translated by the vector \begin{pmatrix}−4\\−3\end{pmatrix}

What are the new coordinates of point S?  (A) (1, 0)  (B) (2, 6)  (C) (1, −6)  (D) (−1, 0)

Jo and Paul are trying to work out an expression for the area of this shape.

Jo says you can do: pr + \frac{(q-p)r}{2}

Paul says you can do: \frac{qr}{2} + \frac{pr}{2}

Who is correct?  (A) Only Jo  (B) Only Paul  (C) Both Jo and Paul  (D) Neither is correct
